{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1659 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "695d79bdc9944e24874e195f11b3a88c60af92d0e619cc2b37b097a330925b03" :edb/db-before-t 1658 :edb/db-after-t 1659 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534971 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:52:33.260Z" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186197738 1078 #edb/ref 17592186197742 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186198448 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446169 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186198449 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446168 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186198978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186198978 1071 "Let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Find $‖Q(x)‖$, where $x = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139534971 17592186045417 false] [17592186198978 1071 "Let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Find $‖Q(x)‖$, where $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186198978 1074 "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nIn this case, since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Q(x)‖ & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186284764 1071 "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$\n- ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal\n- ${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal" 13194139534971 17592186045417 false] [17592186284764 1071 "$$\n{u}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$\n\nII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})\\}$ is orthogonal\n\nIII. $\\{Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})\\}$ is orthonormal" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446170 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446171 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446172 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446173 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1043 #edb/ref 17592186446174 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1045 "Orthogonal Linear Transformations" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1046 #edb/ref 17592186446172 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050910 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446155 1053 #uuid "33e49b6c-0f59-53bc-8c69-4b46de238ff6" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446156 1080 "-2" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446156 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446156 1083 #uuid "1bd4d334-2269-5bfe-a24c-a58aafbef588" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446157 1080 "6" 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446157 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534971 17592186045417 true] [17592186446157 1083 #uuid "4a46d5a3-